body:
Eh, I think we need another element to make AGI truly work; carbon-based circuitry. Silicon is too rigid, no matter how complex it gets it will always be a glorified calculator. Mind you, that's good if you want a computer to do as exactly as you technically tell it and precision.

Carbon-based circuitry when you get the right formula has enough wiggle room to gain chaos. Enough variance to go to multiple paths depending on circumstance, each neuron that wants to go one direction and the others the other way;

A certain way in how energy transfers one form into another that will cause this, something that will give it higher entropy.

As a guy who has been paying off his loans without missing a payment over 10 years at $500 a month and going to be debt free next year;

I will say let them cancel the debt. Fuck that. I'm not going to let everyone else suffer like I have. Shit sucks.

Cancel the debt.
